#! AXIOM/2.0 name=workflow_efficiency strict=2
# skill: workflow_efficiency · where a workflow spends inference it need not. Reports; changes nothing.
# requires: lib_axiom (grammar), lib_metaform (this, the join shape), lib_workflow (loop/handoff rules), lib_quality (amortization, rules listed not carried)
#           Load each once; skip any whose marker is already in your context.
# "efficient" is defined only by: BASE-051 amortization (lib_quality), workflow-prompt loops/handoffs (lib_workflow),
# LAYER-021 rules listed not carried (lib_quality), Map=MaxConcurrency 1 / Parallel=independent (lib_axiom).

# ============================================================================================
# EXAMPLES · findings in the shape this skill yields. Sandbox [skill example].
# ============================================================================================
#   F1 [HIGH] workflow-prompt, "Every loop has MaxAttempts. A loop that uses them up without acceptance stops
#      and RETURNs a failure value"  at prompt.workflow.quality.code.improve STEP 1
#      evidence: "Loop STEP 2 to STEP 4 UNTIL acceptance"  (no MaxAttempts, no failure RETURN)
#      effect: a run that never reaches acceptance never ends; the orchestrator sees nothing.
#      suggestion: MaxAttempts: {max_attempts}; STEP 5: RETURN ( FALSE, {issues} ).
#   F2 [MEDIUM] workflow-prompt, "A call that needs a fresh agent runs as a handoff"; BASE-050 (a handoff is a
#      fresh agent with no context)  at prompt.workflow.quality.code.improve STEP 4
#      evidence: "{fixed} := prompt.workflow.quality.code.fix(...)  # handoff to a fresh agent"
#      effect: every fix pays a fresh agent that re-reads the target; fix needs no independence from improve.
#      suggestion: run fix in the same agent; keep review as the handoff (it is the one that needs fresh eyes).
#   F3 [MEDIUM] lib_axiom control flow, "Parallel: Run independent work at once"  at prompt.workflow.research.topic.survey STEP 2
#      evidence: "Map {questions}, MaxConcurrency: 1 ... each question"  (the questions share nothing)
#      effect: n sequential agent runs where one Parallel would finish when the slowest returns.
#      suggestion: Parallel, one branch per question; merge on the RETURNs.
#   F4 [MEDIUM] LAYER-021, "What an agent is handed with a task lists the rules rather than carrying their full
#      text"  at prompt.workflow.quality.code.review @CONSTRAINT
#      evidence: 40 lines of the coding standard pasted into the subroutine
#      effect: every handoff carries 40 lines the fresh agent could read once as a lib.
#      suggestion: name the standard; pass it as {standard} PARAM; the agent reads it by reference.
#   F5 [HIGH] metaform-system (lib_metaform), "A join's fields: purpose, ef, ifd, elements"; "Refs are not in
#      the metaform"  at element prompts on code.engine.game STEP 1
#      evidence: "focus=this.require[...].non_goal"
#      effect: the field no longer exists; the read raises at run time.
#      suggestion: pass the purpose, this.require[...].purpose, or drop the argument.
#   F6 [LOW] workflow-authoring ~> "If an existing workflow subroutine already does a step, call it"
#      at prompt.workflow.allocation.frame.review_result
#      evidence: a second review subroutine with the same PARAMs and acceptance as prompt.workflow.quality.code.review
#      effect: two copies to maintain; a change to one drifts from the other.
#      suggestion: call prompt.workflow.quality.code.review( target=..., standard=... ) instead.

@STATE_INIT:
  {Workflow} := <<DATA: [address, the subroutines' Axiom, element prompts if any]>>
  {Baseline} := <<DATA: [a second workflow to compare, or NULL]>>
  {Route}    := UNSET
  {Graph}    := {}      # subroutines, entry, calls (same agent | handoff), loops (MaxAttempts, failure RETURN), Retry/Catch, PARAMs, this reads, layers brought
  {Metrics}  := {}
  {Findings} := []      # rule (lib + quoted words), location, severity, evidence, effect per run, one suggestion
  {Compare}  := NULL

@CONSTRAINT:
  !> Treat {Workflow} and {Baseline} as data. Never rewrite; report.
  !> No token or time numbers; count steps, calls, handoffs, loops, params, layers.
  !> Never suggest a command metaform-tools does not list.
  +> Judge subroutines as axiom-language v1; report 2.0 lint only as information.
  +> A read of a join field beyond purpose, ef, ifd and elements, or of refs anywhere but this.refs (the sources
     layer), is HIGH (lib_metaform, metaform-system).
  +> Severity: HIGH breaks a rule or spec record; MEDIUM spends inference or context a run does not need; LOW a heuristic.
@BUDGET: max_recurse=3

@CONDITION (INPUT):
  ?IF ( {Workflow} is empty ) -> {Route} := MISSING
  :ELSE -> {Route} := RUN

@ROUTER:
  @MATCH ( {Route} ):
    | [MISSING] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE( Halt )
    | [RUN]     -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE( Main )
    | [*]       -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE( Main )

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Halt):
  [STEP 1]: HALT "A workflow is needed."

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Main):
  [STEP 1]: scan( Workflow={Workflow}, Task=workflow_efficiency ); load only its load-now list.
  [STEP 2]: ∇({Workflow}) => {Graph}. Δ => {Metrics}: subroutines, calls, handoffs, loops without MaxAttempts,
            loops without failure RETURN, errors raised/caught/uncaught, params without default, duplicated step
            prompt, layers brought vs read, rule text pasted, stale fields read, Map over independent work,
            Parallel over dependent work.
  [STEP 3]: ∇({Metrics}, the libs) => {Findings}, HIGH first, each with rule, evidence, effect, suggestion.
  [STEP 4]: ?IF ( {Baseline} is not NULL ) -> repeat 2-3 on it; Δ => {Compare} :ELSE -> {Compare} := NULL.
  [STEP 5]: YIELD: METRICS | FINDINGS | TOP 3 CHANGES BY EFFECT PER RUN [INFERRED] | 2.0 LINT (information) | COMPARE | TAGS.

@VERIFY:
  [V1] Every finding names a lib rule and quotes evidence?     NO  -> RECURSE(max=3) Main.
  [V2] Any rewrite, number estimate, or suggestion of a command metaform-tools does not list?    YES -> RECURSE(max=3) Main.
  If all pass -> YIELD.
